<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged with the build-setting-generated keys (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES).
  NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription is present for the console link (#1665,
  ADR-0161): iOS shows it right after the in-app consent sheet
  (ConsoleConsentView), never before. NSBonjourServices and any
  com.apple.developer.networking.* entitlement are still deliberately
  absent — multicast discovery awaits Apple's grant of
  com.apple.developer.networking.multicast; the console link is unicast
  only until then.
  Deliberately absent for P0: UIBackgroundModes "audio" (the mic stops when
  the app backgrounds; a "walk mode" would add it later).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Sound Buddy listens through the microphone to estimate your room's tonal balance and suggest EQ changes. Audio is analyzed on this device and never leaves it.</string>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Sound Buddy connects to your X32 or M32 on this network to read channel names, EQ and levels, and changes EQ only when you arm it.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
